    title: "微軟官方 X 帳號遭盜用，用於推廣 Clippy 主題的加密貨幣詐騙",
    summary: "微軟（Microsoft）證實其官方 X 帳號於某日遭未經授權盜用，攻擊者利用該帳號推廣一個以 Clippy 為主題的加密貨幣相關帳號。該帳號甚至更換了微軟的個人頭像，並散播了關於 $Clippy 代幣與 $MSFT 相關的訊息。微軟隨後發布了聲明，澄清其不支持、不認可或不授權任何加密貨幣或相關代幣。微軟發言人指出，該帳號已成功保護，所有未經授權的貼文已移除，並正在調查事件經過。文章分析指出，攻擊者盜用帳號的方式可能包括：透過釣魚頁面騙取帳號密碼、進行 SIM swapping 竊取綁定電話號碼、劫持用於密碼重設的電子郵件，或利用員工設備上的 Infostealer 惡意軟體竊取瀏覽器 Session Cookies，甚至可能是第三方行銷或社群媒體管理工具的漏洞。微軟尚未公開帳號被盜用的具體方式。",
    tags: ["Microsoft", "X 帳號", "加密貨幣詐騙", "帳號盜用", "Infostealer", "SIM swapping"],
    title_en: "Microsoft's Official X Account Hacked and Used to Promote Cryptocurrency Scam Featuring Clippy",
    summary_en: "Microsoft confirmed that its official X account was unauthorizedly compromised on a certain date. Attackers used the account to promote a cryptocurrency-related account themed around Clippy. The account even changed Microsoft's personal profile picture and disseminated information related to the $Clippy and $MSFT tokens. Microsoft subsequently issued a statement clarifying that it does not support, recognize, or authorize any cryptocurrency or related tokens. A Microsoft spokesperson pointed out that the account has been successfully secured, all unauthorized posts have been removed, and an investigation into the incident is underway. The article analyzes that the attackers may have compromised the account through methods such as: phishing pages to steal account passwords, SIM swapping to steal linked phone numbers, hijacking emails used for password resets, or exploiting Infostealer malware on employee devices to steal browser Session Cookies, or even vulnerabilities in third-party marketing or social media management tools. Microsoft has not yet disclosed the specific method of the account compromise.",
    tags_en: ["Microsoft", "X Account", "Cryptocurrency Scam", "Account Compromise", "Infostealer", "SIM swapping"],
