    title: "Apache Directory LDAP API 存在 CVE-2026-102731 漏洞：過度記憶體分配導致拒絕服務",
    summary: "Apache Directory LDAP API 存在一個嚴重的記憶體分配漏洞，編號為 CVE-2026-102731。此漏洞影響版本為 1.2.0 到 1.2.9 之前的版本。攻擊者（或中間人）可以發送一個經過 BER 編碼的、看似較小的回應，但會導致伺服器在接收到任何資料前，執行過大的記憶體分配。這可能觸發 OutOfMemoryError，進而造成服務拒絕（Denial of Service, DoS）。此問題特別影響未設定 MAX_PDU_SIZE_ATTR 的嵌入式伺服器。建議使用者立即升級至 1.2.9 版本，以修復此漏洞。",
    tags: ["Apache Directory LDAP API", "CVE-2026-102731", "LDAP", "Denial of Service", "記憶體分配"],
    title_en: "Apache Directory LDAP API has CVE-2026-102731 vulnerability: Excessive memory allocation causes Denial of Service",
    summary_en: "Apache Directory LDAP API contains a critical memory allocation vulnerability, identified as CVE-2026-102731. This vulnerability affects versions prior to 1.2.0 through 1.2.9. An attacker (or man-in-the-middle) can send a seemingly small, BER-encoded response that causes the server to perform excessive memory allocation before receiving any data. This may trigger an OutOfMemoryError, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS). This issue particularly affects embedded servers where MAX_PDU_SIZE_ATTR is not configured. Users are advised to immediately upgrade to version 1.2.9 to patch this vulnerability.",
    tags_en: ["Apache Directory LDAP API", "CVE-2026-102731", "LDAP", "Denial of Service", "Memory Allocation"],
