    title_en: "Home Widget 1.10 Major Update: Provides One-Click HomeKit Camera Viewing and Whole-House Lighting Control",
    summary_en: "Home Widget is a third-party application designed to optimize the Apple HomeKit control experience. Because the native Apple Home app has a complex interface structure, users often require too many steps during daily operation. Home Widget addresses this pain point by creating a custom Control Panel. The main update in version 1.10 is the 'camera mosaic,' which allows users to view all HomeKit cameras in a single scrolling view by clicking a widget on the Home Screen or Lock Screen, greatly improving monitoring efficiency. Furthermore, this version adds direct widget control for thermostats, allowing users to adjust whole-house lighting or set the home temperature without entering the Home app or calling Siri. These features fill a practical gap between widgets and native applications, enabling users to manage large HomeKit device setups more quickly. Additionally, 1.10 supports the native iOS 26/27 widget appearance and expands support for more heating systems, such as HeaterCooler.",
    tags_en: ["HomeKit", "Home Widget", "iOS", "Smart Home", "Apple Watch", "Control Panel"],
