    title: "Apple 調整 macOS 隱私權設定，限制第三方 AI 應用程式濫用權限存取訊息紀錄",
    summary: "由於第三方 AI 代理人（AI agents）可能濫用應用程式權限，存取用戶的私密資料，Apple 宣布將修改 macOS 的隱私權設定。此議題源於科技評論家 Jason Aten 的案例，他指出 Meta 的 AI 代理 Muse 似乎在未經明確授權的情況下，能讀取其 Apple Messages 的對話紀錄。雖然 Meta 方面（透過 CTO David Singleton）反駁稱，Muse 存取 Messages 內容必須用戶手動開啟「Full Disk Access」（全碟存取）和啟用 Messages 連接器，但 macOS 安全專家 Patrick Wardle 質疑，若已授予 Full Disk Access，理論上任何非 root 檔案內容都應可讀取。為防止 AI 應用程式過度存取用戶的日曆、電子郵件、訊息等敏感資源，Apple 採取此舉，旨在提高系統層級的隱私保護，避免資料被惡意或過度使用。",
    tags: ["macOS", "Apple Messages", "Full Disk Access", "AI Agents", "隱私權", "Meta", "Muse"],
    title_en: "Apple Adjusts macOS Privacy Settings to Limit Third-Party AI App Misuse of Message Records",
    summary_en: "Due to the potential for third-party AI agents to misuse application permissions and access users' private data, Apple announced changes to macOS privacy settings. This issue was highlighted by tech critic Jason Aten, who pointed out that Meta's AI agent, Muse, appeared to read his Apple Messages conversation history without explicit authorization. Although Meta (via CTO David Singleton) refuted this, stating that Muse accessing Messages content requires the user to manually enable 'Full Disk Access' and activate the Messages connector, macOS security expert Patrick Wardle questioned that if Full Disk Access is granted, theoretically any non-root file content should be readable. To prevent AI applications from excessively accessing sensitive resources such as the user's calendar, email, and messages, Apple is taking this measure to enhance system-level privacy protection and prevent data from being misused or accessed excessively.",
