    summary_en: "Google Messages recently pushed a major update, introducing a completely redesigned long-press menu to the chat conversation interface. This update aims to provide a more intuitive interaction experience by placing frequently used functions in prominent locations. Key improvements include support for both light and dark themes, along with optimizations for landscape screen modes to ensure the menu is easy to operate. The most notable feature is 'Precise Copying': users can now long-press a message, then long-press the text content to select a specific portion using a draggable handle, and subsequently choose to copy, translate, or select all. Furthermore, when long-pressing a chat message or image, the floating menu displays functions such as Remix (for photos), Reply, Forward, Copy (text), Favorite, Delete, More Options, Info, and Save (for photos). This new feature has been observed to be widely rolled out, with the stable version being 20260910_03_RC02. Users who have not enabled it are advised to force stop the application via app information to ensure proper functionality.",
