    title_en: "Google Releases Android 17 QPR3 Beta 1: Adding Notes Quick Settings Tile and Gemini Intelligence Features",
    summary_en: "Google recently released Android 17 QPR3 Beta 1, serving as the latest preview update toward the stable version expected in March 2027. This update primarily targets devices like the Pixel 11 series and introduces a Notes Quick Settings Tile, allowing users to access note-taking functions more conveniently. Furthermore, after installing this Beta version, the Pixel 10 series displays a Gemini Intelligence animation on its boot animation, and the system settings have incorporated a Proactive Assistance feature. This update also fixes multiple system stability issues, including application crashes when launched from the Quick Settings Tile, NFC service crashes after detecting a tag on Android 16, and various device freezing or crashing issues related to fingerprint and face unlock. While these Beta updates provide developers and early adopters with the latest system features and stability patches, users should note that this remains a testing version, and features and stability may change in subsequent updates.",
