    title: "美國逮捕嫌犯：指控利用假文件走私價值超過 3 億美元的 Nvidia 晶片至中國",
    summary: "美國司法部（DOJ）宣布逮捕嫌犯 Greg Lui，指控其利用偽造文件走私高階電腦伺服器，其中包含受出口管制（export-controlled）的 Nvidia 晶片至中國。Lui 據稱是 Earthmade Computer 的執行長，與馬來西亞和新加坡等地的貨運代理公司勾結，非法轉運晶片。被走私的晶片包括 Nvidia 的 A100 和 H100 GPU，這些晶片雖然並非最先進型號，但具備處理大量數據和訓練大型語言模型的能力。美國政府擔心，如果中國突然獲得足夠的晶片，可能對其 AI 或軍事能力構成國家安全風險。指控顯示，該走私計畫從 2023 年 10 月開始，持續至 2026 年 8 月。證據包括 2024 年的電子郵件和銀行記錄，顯示走私者多次偽造目的地和購買文件，將原本標記為目的地為馬來西亞的伺服器，最終轉運至中國的企業。此事件涉及美國出口管制法規，屬於國際貿易與國家安全層面的問題。",
    tags: ["Nvidia", "A100", "H100", "美國出口管制", "國家安全", "晶片走私"],
    title_en: "US Arrests Suspect Accused of Smuggling Nvidia Chips Worth Over $300 Million to China",
    summary_en: "The U.S. Department of Justice (DOJ) announced the arrest of suspect Greg Lui, who is accused of using falsified documents to smuggle high-end computer servers containing export-controlled Nvidia chips into China. Lui, reportedly the CEO of Earthmade Computer, allegedly colluded with freight forwarding companies in locations such as Malaysia and Singapore to illegally transship the chips. The smuggled chips included Nvidia's A100 and H100 GPUs. Although these chips are not the most advanced models, they possess the capability to process massive amounts of data and train large language models. The U.S. government is concerned that China gaining sufficient chips could pose a national security risk to its AI or military capabilities. The charges indicate that the smuggling operation began in October 2023 and continued until August 2026. Evidence includes 2024 emails and bank records showing the smugglers repeatedly falsified destination and purchase documents, ultimately transshipping servers originally marked for Malaysia to companies in China. This incident involves U.S. export control regulations and falls under the scope of international trade and national security issues.",
